From 7700d73b8359248b1aabe96221e32be72e6de99f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:53:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: thread-local pages in 16 KiB groups (fastmem); native
 functions found in every code region; native memcmp

Thread-local pages (KThreadLocalPage, under EDEN_ARENA_LINE_UP) come four at a time from a
16 KiB group of the system pool, back to back and aligned, mapped as ThreadLocal at a 16 KiB
boundary (KProcess::AllocateGroupedThreadLocalPage / FreeGroupedThreadLocalPage): the PS4's
fastmem arena maps 16 KiB at a time, so a page on its own never lined up and every
TPIDRRO_EL0-based access walked the page table (14% of Silksong's hot samples were in blocks
reading thread-local storage). A group keeps its allocation's reference until it is unmapped
with its last page; a failed allocation falls back to a page of its own, as before.

Native functions (native_functions.h): every ReadExecute Code/AliasCode region is tried, not
only modules Core::FindModules names (Silksong's copies weren't found); the symbol count comes
from DT_HASH or DT_GNU_HASH when the strings don't follow the symbols; a symbol of no type
inside the module's code counts; the optimized-routines names (__memcpy_aarch64...) and, 32-bit,
the ARM EABI's __aeabi_memcpy/__aeabi_memmove (4/8). memcmp (kind 4) runs natively too
(dynarmic's NativeMemcmp callback, A64 and A32; Eden's Compare: the first differing bytes'
difference, as the SDK's).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
